          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose gas when the lawn is big, the grass grows thick or often gets ahead of you, or you would rather not think about battery runtime at all. A push mower suits a small, level yard; anything larger calls for a self-propelled model, with rear-wheel drive if there are hills. The Toro Super Recycler and Recycler lead this list, and the Craftsman M115 and Troy-Bilt TB110 cover the tightest budgets.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The routine matters more than the badge on the hood. Fresh fuel, an oil change every season, a new plug and filter, a sharp blade and careful winter storage are what keep a gas mower starting on the first or second pull, year after year.
